ZBazar allows customers to buy items with multiple stackable adjustments applied to their shopping cart. For the holiday season, a customer's base shopping cart price can have a flat RamadanDiscountDecorator, a percentage-based VATTaxDecorator, and a fixed-rate DeliveryFeeDecorator layered onto it simultaneously.
The Problem (The Exam Trap)In standard implementations of the Decorator pattern, wrappers calculate costs in whatever arbitrary order they are nested at runtime. However, financial rules dictate a strict sequence of operations regardless of how the client constructs the object:Discounts must always be applied first to the base price.VAT Tax must be calculated after the discount has been deducted.Delivery Fees must be added last, as delivery charges are legally non-taxable.
Technical RequirementsDynamic Customization (Decorator Pattern): Design a unified system where any combinations of discounts, taxes, and handling fees can be layered onto a base shopping cart dynamically.Priority Execution Enforcement: Implement a strategy where the decorators automatically execute their calculations according to business priority sequence (Discount \(\rightarrow \) Tax \(\rightarrow \) Delivery), completely neutralizing nesting errors by the client.
